03-22-why-i-love-nixos.html\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47479751\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47479751\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 159\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 126\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://www.birkey.co/2026-03-22-why-i-love-nixos.html","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47479751","date_published":"2026-03-22T17:17:06Z","author":{"name":"birkey","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=birkey"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47479627","title":"Five Years of Running a Systems Reading Group at Microsoft","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://armaansood.com/posts/systems-reading-group/\"\u003ehttps://armaansood.com/posts/systems-reading-group/\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47479627\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47479627\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 105\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 28\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://armaansood.com/posts/systems-reading-group/","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47479627","date_published":"2026-03-22T17:06:38Z","author":{"name":"Foe","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=Foe"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47479183","title":"GrapheneOS refuses to comply with new age verification laws for operating system","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://www.tomshardware.com/software/operating-systems/grapheneos-refuses-to-comply-with-age-verification-laws\"\u003ehttps://www.tomshardware.com/software/operating-systems/grapheneos-refuses-to-comply-with-age-verification-laws\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47479183\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47479183\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 192\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 98\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://www.tomshardware.com/software/operating-systems/grapheneos-refuses-to-comply-with-age-verification-laws","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47479183","date_published":"2026-03-22T16:28:52Z","author":{"name":"CrypticShift","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=CrypticShift"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47479115","title":"Ask HN: Apple terminated our dev account over a rogue employee","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eI know that HN isn't a customer support forum and it might not be right to post this here, but we are absolutely desperate and hoping someone in this community can point us in the right direction.\u003cp\u003eWe are a small software company in Africa. For over two years, we've built and maintained an app. It has become a vital economic engine for our local community, employing a whole fleet of delivery agents and serving as a lifeline for local stores and restaurants.\u003cp\u003eRecently, we discovered that a single employee used a shared company machine to engage in unauthorized activities that violated Apple's Developer Terms of Service.\u003cp\u003eWe took immediate action: we fired the employee on the spot and completely overhauled our security. We revoked all individual access and implemented mandatory, peer-reviewed, supervised sessions for any Apple Developer portal access.\u003cp\u003eThe problem is the collateral damage. Apple terminated our entire organization's account. We submitted an appeal through App Store Connect, but we feel completely stuck behind automated walls. We have also emailed Apple executives, but are waiting in the dark.\u003cp\u003eBecause of this one employee's actions, our app is facing total removal, and families in our community are quite literally losing their daily income. We aren't asking for special treatment, just a chance for a real human at App Review to look at the security steps we've taken and consider a second chance.\u003cp\u003eIf anyone here has been through this, has advice, or knows how to get a human at Apple to actually read our appeal, our entire community would be forever grateful. Thank you so much for your time.\u003cp\u003e(For reference if any Apple folks are reading: our Apple Team ID is T35TM9SW45)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47479115\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47479115\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 128\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 30\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47479115","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47479115","date_published":"2026-03-22T16:23:50Z","author":{"name":"0x1f","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=0x1f"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47478687","title":"MAUI Is Coming to Linux","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://avaloniaui.net/blog/maui-avalonia-preview-1\"\u003ehttps://avaloniaui.net/blog/maui-avalonia-preview-1\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47478687\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47478687\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 140\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 66\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://avaloniaui.net/blog/maui-avalonia-preview-1","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47478687","date_published":"2026-03-22T15:43:21Z","author":{"name":"DeathArrow","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=DeathArrow"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47478579","title":"Atlassian says it had right to fire engineer for suggesting CEO is 'rich jerk'","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-03-16/atlassian-defends-firing-worker-who-suggested-ceo-is-rich-jerk\"\u003ehttps://www.